{"custom_id": "f6a355df0f0033faa21630230c11ce56ba360f7f8ae672ed", "meta": {"loop": "topk4L02", "task": "annotate_with_guidelines", "occurrence": 0, "attempt": 0, "max_tokens": 128000, "prompt_sha256": "d27fe0d272797789ccb10a9861e274e6bdac943c30f8dea88df47f25ef8c1582", "prompt_chars": 70661}, "batch_id": "msgbatch_01438JrwSD1FeRYincbckVb2", "saved_utc": "2026-10-23T11:51:54+00:00", "message": {"id": "msg_011CgK7Zk5bMUM3gxuvZvhSZ", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":37,\"end\":50,\"text\":\"C9 deficiency\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Deficit-named disorder in premodifier form (molecular name C9 plus head deficiency) that names one disorder and is not used prenominally in the title. It is the head of its phrase, so it is a Specific Disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 1: Deficiency-type nominals with a molecular complement; Section 1 Specific Disease (premodifier-form deficit disorder)\"},{\"start\":101,\"end\":113,\"text\":\"C9-deficient\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"Adjectival form of a deficit-named disorder used as a prenominal modifier of the noun subject. Adjectival deficiency forms are Modifiers, not Specific Diseases.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 1 Rule B(i) (adjectival or participial form); Section 3 Prenominal disease names\"},{\"start\":694,\"end\":707,\"text\":\"C9 deficiency\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"Deficit-named disorder used prenominally before the gene head noun genes. The gene head does not change the label, so it is a Modifier.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 3 Prenominal disease names (deficit-named disorders used prenominally; gene-head modifiers)\"},{\"start\":977,\"end\":993,\"text\":\"deficiency of C9\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Deficiency-type nominal whose complement is the gene product C9. The subject is a case-specific patient described as heterozygous for the deficiency, an inherited trait, so Rule B applies and the whole head-plus-complement nominal is labeled. The determiner complete is outside the span.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 1 Deficiency-type nominals with a molecular complement, Rule B and of-argument boundary (context-licensed condition)\"},{\"start\":1074,\"end\":1087,\"text\":\"C9 deficiency\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Deficit-named disorder in premodifier form used as the clausal subject of a generic statement about its prevalence. It is not prenominal, so it is a standalone Specific Disease.\",\"guideline_section\":\"Section 1 Deficiency-type nominals with a molecular complement (premodifier form, Specific Disease)\"}]}", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 25334, "output_tokens": 15838, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 15059}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}